<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siem Reap</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syiem">Siem</a> Reap is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>, capital of Siem Reap Province, near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a>. The province was ruled by Siam from the late 18th century until the Franco-Siamese treaty of 1907 returned it to Cambodia under French protection. The city grew as the gateway to Angkor and is now the centre of Cambodia's tourism industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siem-reap.jpg" alt="Siem Reap" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willuconquer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_porch_of_Wat_Damnak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
